        {
            "id": 72,
            "title": "Qarraba Cliffs",
            "description": "Qarraba Cliffs, also known as Il-Qarraba, is a dramatic coastal headland on Malta’s north-west coast between Għajn Tuffieħa Bay and Ġnejna Bay. This spot is known for its raw cliff views, clay slopes, rugged paths, and wide open views over the Mediterranean. It forms part of one of Malta’s most scenic coastal walks, connecting Golden Bay, Għajn Tuffieħa, Qarraba and Ġnejna Bay. The route is beautiful but exposed, with uneven ground and steep sections, so it is best explored with proper shoes and extra care, especially on windy days or after rain.",
